---
import InstitutionalPage from "../../components/InstitutionalPage.astro";

const SITE = import.meta.env.SITE || "https://canapalandia.com";
const canonical = `${SITE}/en/about-us/`;
---

<InstitutionalPage
  title="About Canapalandia | Independent hemp and cannabis information"
  description="Canapalandia is an independent editorial project covering hemp, CBD, cannabis policy, research and culture. We do not operate an online store or sell products directly."
  canonical={canonical}
  eyebrow="Canapalandia since 2016"
  heading="Independent information about hemp, cannabis policy and culture"
  lead="Canapalandia is an independent editorial project. We publish news, explainers, guides and tools to help readers understand a complex and fast-changing field without presenting editorial information as a sales pitch or medical advice."
  currentLabel="About us"
>
  <section>
    <h2>What Canapalandia is today</h2>
    <p>
      Canapalandia is an online editorial project focused on industrial hemp, CBD,
      cannabis policy, research, sustainability and culture. We do not operate an
      online store, process product orders or sell cannabis- or hemp-based products
      directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our goal is to make technical and controversial topics easier to understand,
      while separating facts, sources, interpretation and opinion as clearly as
      possible.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where the project comes from</h2>
    <p>
      Canapalandia started in 2016 as a blog about hemp and cannabis culture. The
      project has gone through different phases, including an earlier commercial
      experience. Today its main role is editorial: informing, explaining and
      building useful tools for readers.
    </p>
    <p class="institutional-note">
      Some older English pages and articles belong to previous phases of the
      project and are progressively reviewed when they no longer represent the
      current Canapalandia.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We prioritize primary sources, official documents and scientific studies when available.</li>
      <li>We add dates and context when laws, research or news may change over time.</li>
      <li>We distinguish editorial content from commercial collaborations.</li>
      <li>We update or correct content when better information becomes available.</li>
      <li>Our content is not medical or legal advice.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Commercial relationships and transparency</h2>
    <p>
      Canapalandia may support its editorial work through advertising, sponsored
      content, selected partnerships, affiliate links and voluntary reader support.
      Commercial collaborations must be identifiable and should not determine the
      conclusions of independent editorial coverage.
    </p>
    <p>
      Paid and affiliate links are qualified appropriately. Companies and projects
      interested in editorial collaborations can review our
      <a href="/pubblicita/">advertising and partnership options</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Information first</h2>
    <p>
      We do not promise therapeutic results, certify the legality or safety of a
      product, or replace professional medical or legal advice. Our role is to give
      readers clearer context, better sources and practical ways to understand the
      information available to them.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the current Italian editorial profile, visit
      <a href="/chi-siamo/">Chi siamo</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</InstitutionalPage>
